<title>USA: Fidelity Federal sees staff cuts adding $0.44/shr.</title>
<headline>Fidelity Federal sees staff cuts adding $0.44/shr.</headline>
<dateline>EVANSVILLE, Ind. 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fidelity Federal Bancorp said Friday it expects staff cuts it recently made to save the company about $2 million pre-tax or $0.44 a share after tax.</p>
<p>The bank holding company cut about 35 positions in the last three months through restructuring and attrition, chief financial officer Donald Neel said.</p>
<p>Earlier Friday, the company reported net income of $529,000, or $0.20 a share for the third quarter ended March 31, compared to net income of $569,000, or $0.20 a share, a year ago.</p>
<p>Fidelity Federal shares closed unchanged at 7-3/4 Friday.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
